; The question, kept apart from the puzzle (Prologue wish 12).
(load "stdlib.pol")

; `possible` is enough: its witness IS a solution, printed as the eight moves
; that place the queens. Asking for a LIST of all 92 is a query's job, not a
; property's — and `pol check` already reports each complete placement as a
; dead end, since a full board has no move left.
(property solvable "all eight queens placed, none attacking"
  (possible (all (q queen) (defined q.at))))
